; A CURRENCY:NUMBER option takes any Unicode decimal digit, as Python's \d
; and Decimal do: USD's default tolerance is 0.5 (Arabic-Indic digits), so
; the transaction balances.
option "inferred_tolerance_default" "USD:٠.٥"
option "display_precision" "USD:٠.٠١"

2020-01-01 open Assets:A
2020-01-01 open Assets:B

2020-01-02 * "Residual within the configured tolerance"
  Assets:A   1 USD
  Assets:B  -1.4 USD
